menu "RoboHub Common"

config ROBOHUB_COMMON
    bool "Enable RoboHub Common Core"
    default y
    help
        Core interfaces, HAL abstractions, registry, platform contract.
        This module is always enabled and required by all platforms.

config RH_PRODUCTION
    bool "Production build (security hardening; some steps are irreversible)"
    default n
    help
        Builds the image with the platform's production preset: on an ESP32,
        flash encryption (release mode), secure boot v2 and NVS encryption; on
        an RP2350, a signed image and the OTP file that enables secure boot;
        on an STM32, nothing changes in the image, and `rho flash --production`
        sets read-out protection level 1.

        Off by default, and nothing irreversible happens at build time. The
        irreversible steps (eFuses, OTP) happen only when the image is flashed
        with `rho flash --production`, which prints every one of them and asks
        for the board's name to be typed first, or - on an ESP32 - when the
        production image first boots. See each platform's docs and
        robohub/docs/doc/architecture/security.md ("Production builds").

endmenu
